### Project Methods Overview
These are the results of a pilot study of eDNA in Cook Inlet from Nov. 2020 to Nov. 2021. This pilot project consisted of two eDNA sample collections paired with visual CIB surveys: 

1. Monthly samples were collected at two sites at two depths each (0m & 5m) in the Kenai River across the year,  

2. Higher frequency sampling (sub-weekly/biweekly) of 20 Mile River was conducted from August 2021-Nov. 2021 at the surface (0m)

We successfully designed and implemented sample collection and processing methodologies to track Beluga and their prey. We specifically applied qPCR assays for Beluga, Coho, Chinook, and Eulachon (*Thaleichthys pacificus*) and vertebrate community metabarcoding assays (MiFish 12S) to all eDNA samples. All samples were collected at high tide when Beluga are known to enter river systems [@moore2000beluga].
  
