4. Although we demonstrate successful eDNA sample processing, the high sediment load of Cook Inlet waters posed a significant challenge to water filtration. Here we deployed 1 µm filters to filter 1 L samples which took up to 2 hours to filter given the high sediment load (0.6µm sediment). For future deployments **we recommend the utilization of 5µm eDNA filters** which should ease the filtration burden and have been found to collect sufficient marine vertebrate eDNA [@power2023environmental].  

# Visual, Metabarcoding, & qPCR Detection Comparisons

## Twentymile River Results 

**Note this is the focus of the study and the highlight results.**

#### Beluga Observations: Visual vs. eDNA Metabarcoding vs. qPCR. 
eDNA and visual observations of Cook Inlet Beluga whales were largely concordant within Turnagain Arm (Figure 1). eDNA detections at 20 Mile River occurred during when Beluga were only visually observed at 93.5 Mile Marker and were heard to be along the 1 West of Hope (~20km from the mouth of Twentymile River). This strongly suggests that Beluga eDNA is being transported >20 km by tidal bores in the second largest tidal exchange system on Earth.

#### Figure 3. Visual and eDNA detections of beluga occurrence in Turnagain Arm. 

```{r,qPCR_4_species,echo=FALSE,message=FALSE,warning=FALSE,fig.align = "center", fig.height = 8, fig.width = 6,out.width = "8.5in"}

# Pull in qPCR Data
qPCR_AK_data_with_model <- readRDS(file=here("analysis","qPCR_AK_data_with_model.RDS"))

dilution <- 1

# Clean up qPCR data for merging and format dates/values
qPCR_AK_data_with_model %>% 
  #filter(., `Sample Name`!="" & Sample.Name !="") %>% 
  filter(., `Target Name` %in% c("cetacea", "Chinook" , "Coho"   ,  "Eulachon")) %>% 
  filter(., Task =="UNKNOWN") %>% 
    filter(., !is.na(LabID)) %>% 
   filter(., !is.na(Volume)) %>% 
  filter(., !str_detect(New_name_no_tech,"Diet")) %>% 
  filter(., Sample_Control == "Sample") %>% 
    mutate(., Sample_date = as.Date(Sample_date,"%m/%d/%y")) %>% 
  mutate(., Tide_height = as.numeric(Tide_height)) %>%  
   mutate(., Quantity = as.numeric(str_remove_all(Quantity,","))) %>%
  mutate(Quantity = if_else(CT=="Undetermined", 0, Quantity)) %>% 
    mutate(Quantity = if_else(CT >40, 0, Quantity)) %>% 
        mutate(Quantity = if_else(is.na(Quantity), 0, Quantity)) %>% 
     mutate(mean_dnacopy_L = dilution*(100/(Volume/2))*10^mean,
            q2.5_dnacopy_L = dilution*(100/(Volume/2))*10^q2.5,
            q97.5_dnacopy_L = dilution*(100/(Volume/2))*10^q97.5,
            q25_dnacopy_L = dilution*(100/(Volume/2))*10^q25,
            q75_dnacopy_L = dilution*(100/(Volume/2))*10^q75,
            ) %>% 
            mutate(mean_dnacopy_L = if_else(Quantity==0, 0, mean_dnacopy_L)) -> qPCR_4_species

# Save processed qPCR data
saveRDS(qPCR_4_species,here("analysis","Output","qPCR_4_species.RDS"))
```

