# Beluga occurrence in Twentymile River correlated with Coho salmon run timing

We demonstrate that eDNA metabarcoding can successfully capture changes in fish assemblages on a sub-weekly time scale, allowing for comparison of Beluga habitat use against anadromous fish run timing. Specifically, we find that Beluga occurrence in Twentymile River was strongly correlated with increases in Coho abundances in summer/fall 2021 (Figure 4 & Figures S1-S3). 


